{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1108538-solar-protection-charms-based-on-two-solar-attack-charms","id":1108538,"title":"Solar protection Charms, based on two Solar attack Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-27T16:05:37-07:00","id":1108538,"title":"Solar protection Charms, based on two Solar attack Charms","content":"What do y'all think of these inversions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FADING LIGHT QUICKENING (Nimble Reaving Wind)</b><br /> <i>1m; Reflexive, Instant; No Keywords; </i><i>Melee 1, Essence 1 \u2013 No Prerequisites</i><br /> <br /> She may use this Charm on her turn to move away from a target without using a disengage action, so long as she uses her movement to enter close range with another target for whom she uses the Defend Other action. However, that target must be himself be embattled by at least two opponents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PERFECT BLADE AEGIS</b> <b>(Thunderclap Rush Attack)</b><br /> <i>3m; Reflexive, Instant; No Keywords; Melee 3, Essence 1 \u2013 No Prerequisites</i><br /> <br /> The Solar ignores her position in the Initiative order, crossing one range band to perform a Defend Other action for a target who is not within close range of her, but who is embattled by at least one opponent. The Solar must be able to cross the distance. Even if her ward is being targeted by someone using an effect like Solar Thunderclap Rush Attack, she automatically acts first.<br /> <br /> The range of this Charm may be extended by other effects that supplement move actions.<br /> <br /> The movement of this Charm does not count as the Solar's movement action for her turn, save that she cannot make a normal reflexive Move action. She may flurry her Defend Other action with any other permissible action, and is explicitly allowed to combine the effect of this Charm with War Lion Stance.<br /> <br /> At Melee 5, Essence 3+, the character may add one Willpower to the cost of this Charm to transfer (Essence or 5, whichever is lower) Initiative from herself to her ward.<br /> <br /> This Charm can be used once per target, per scene, but can be refreshed against a single target the next time that they recover from Initiative Crash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FINAL SUNSET STANCE</b><br /> <i>\u2014; Permanent; Perilous; Melee 3, Essence 1 \u2013 Perfect Blade Aegis</i><br /> <br /> This Charm upgrades Perfect Blade Aegis. The Solar may now rush to the defense of a character who is not embattled, but against whom an opponent is making a ranged attack. To do this, the Solar must spend the Willpower point to lose the full amount of Initiative she might have otherwise been able to transfer to her ward, who does not receive it.<br /> <br /> (Note that the Perilous keyword prevents the Solar from using this Charm while crashed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T04:17:54-07:00","id":1110508,"title":"","content":"I realized something that makes Fading Light Quickening NOT equal to Nimble Reaving Wind.<br /> <br /> When a Solar uses Nimble Reaving Wind, he's trading one danger for another, because both the character he flees and the character he approaches are enemies. Even after moving, the Solar is still embattled and would need to use a Disengage action to retreat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FADING LIGHT QUICKENING (Nimble Reaving Wind)</b><br /> <i>1m; Reflexive, Instant; No Keywords; </i><i>Melee 1, Essence 1 \u2013 No Prerequisites</i><br /> <br /> She may use this Charm on her turn to move away from a target without using a disengage action, so long as she uses her movement to enter close range with another target for whom she uses the Defend Other action. <b>However, that target must be himself be embattled by at least two opponents.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> This revision preserves the equality between the original and custom Charms. Just as with Nimble Reaving Wind, the Solar is traveling from danger to danger. Seeing one of her allies outnumbered is also an excellent justification for how the Solar can be inspired to leap to their defense like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perfect Blade Aegis currently has a similar problem, since it can also be used as an escape in a way that Thunderclap Rush Attack cannot, while still being just as much of an approaching method.<br /> <br /> In this case, I think the additional clause only needs to require that ONE opponent is within close range of the character the Solar intends to protect. And there could definitely be an upgrade Charm that relaxes that restriction, so that the Solar can leap to defend someone targeted just by a single ranged attack, after which the Solar and her ward can begin to freely retreat.<br /> <br /> On the balance, this upgraded effect probably should require the Solar to pay the Initiative she would have otherwise given to her ward, who doesn't receive it, either.<br /> <br /> It should also have the Perilous keyword, so that the Solar cannot use this effect while crashed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-02-2017, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}